ll-at-1-99-million-then-fetched-2-9-million-in-cash-city-records-now-flag-the-transaction-as-unusual/articleshow/136171929.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-washington-home-owned-by-us-congresswoman-elise-stefaniks-family-failed-to-sell-at-1-99-million-then-fetched-2-9-million-in-cash-city-records-now-flag-the-transaction-as-unusual/articleshow/136171929.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T02:04:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136172299,imgsize-1186721.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Lululemon founder Chip Wilson says Canadian women aren't having as many babies as men want; some men may need to import brides from Thailand]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136172138.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/lululemon-founder-chip-wilson-says-canadian-women-arent-having-as-many-babies-as-men-want-some-men-may-need-to-import-brides-from-thailand/articleshow/136172138.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/lululemon-founder-chip-wilson-says-canadian-women-arent-having-as-many-babies-as-men-want-some-men-may-need-to-import-brides-from-thailand/articleshow/136172138.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T01:31:25+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136172168,imgsize-49148.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Bournemouth residents oppose two new padel courts, citing noise and swearing from existing courts]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136171836.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Residents near West Hants Club are voicing opposition to proposed new padel courts due to existing noise issues. They report constant disturbances from shouts and sounds that disrupt their daily lives and enjoyment of outdoor spaces. Complaints have been made to BCP Council regarding noise levels and offensive language from players. The club claims it operates responsibly, with measures to manage noise and ensure member behavior.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/residents-living-near-1-million-homes-in-bournemouth-say-a-private-tennis-clubs-padel-courts-bring-constant-noise-and-swearing-they-are-fighting-a-proposal-for-two-more-floodlit-courts-close-to-gardens/articleshow/136171836.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/residents-living-near-1-million-homes-in-bournemouth-say-a-private-tennis-clubs-padel-courts-bring-constant-noise-and-swearing-they-are-fighting-a-proposal-for-two-more-floodlit-courts-close-to-gardens/articleshow/136171836.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T01:00:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136171911,imgsize-2211641.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Egypt highway inferno kills 30 after fuel tanker overturns]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136171820.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A harrowing event unfolded in Giza's Al-Warraq district when a vehicle turned over and burst into flames. Tragically, over 30 individuals perished, while another 15 suffered injuries. Emergency services quickly arrived at the scene to extinguish the blaze and offer medical assistance. The incident took place on a major ring road in Greater Cairo, raising renewed concerns about the pressing issues of road safety in Egypt.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/30-killed-15-injured-in-deadly-blaze-on-cairo-ring-road-after-fuel-vehicle-overturns/articleshow/136171820.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/30-killed-15-injured-in-deadly-blaze-on-cairo-ring-road-after-fuel-vehicle-overturns/articleshow/136171820.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T00:56:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136171841,imgsize-238834.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Chinese scientist, Arizona State University assistant professor, says he does not know why he was arrested by ICE: 'I still have nightmares']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136171792.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/chinese-scientist-arizona-state-university-assistant-professor-says-he-does-not-know-why-he-was-arrested-by-ice-i-still-have-nightmares/articleshow/136171792.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/chinese-scientist-arizona-state-university-assistant-professor-says-he-does-not-know-why-he-was-arrested-by-ice-i-still-have-nightmares/articleshow/136171792.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T00:53:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136171828,imgsize-140096.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Michigan widow's $78m truck crash award cut by $24m as court orders retrial on $19m claim]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136171612.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Michigan appeals court overturned a $24 million award for pre-impact fright in a wrongful death case. The court ruled that state law does not allow compensation for fear experienced before injury. A new trial has been ordered for the $19 million awarded for conscious pain and suffering. The trial originally awarded over $78 million for the negligence of an 18-wheel lorry driver.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-michigan-widow-once-won-more-than-78-million-after-a-truck-crash-killed-her-husband-and-son-an-appeals-court-has-now-thrown-out-24-million-for-their-pre-impact-fear-and-ordered-a-retrial-on-19-million/articleshow/136171612.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-michigan-widow-once-won-more-than-78-million-after-a-truck-crash-killed-her-husband-and-son-an-appeals-court-has-now-thrown-out-24-million-for-their-pre-impact-fear-and-ordered-a-retrial-on-19-million/articleshow/136171612.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T00:53:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136171823,imgsize-1842179.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Alberta family donates 160 acres of native prairie for conservation while allowing cattle grazing]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136171418.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A remarkable commitment to conservation has been made by a ranching family in southern Alberta, who have donated 160 acres of untouched prairie land for long-term protection. This initiative allows cattle grazing to persist while maintaining the delicate balance of the native grassland ecosystem. For nearly a century, the Coppieters family has managed this land, protecting its agricultural history.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-1925-a-canadian-family-began-farming-in-southern-alberta-101-years-later-descendants-have-donated-160-acres-of-native-grassland-that-will-remain-protected-while-ranchers-continue-grazing-cattle/articleshow/136171418.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-1925-a-canadian-family-began-farming-in-southern-alberta-101-years-later-descendants-have-donated-160-acres-of-native-grassland-that-will-remain-protected-while-ranchers-continue-grazing-cattle/articleshow/136171418.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T00:29:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136171601,imgsize-2178564.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Man buys back his 1972 Lotus Europa 35 years after selling it during divorce]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136156814.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-man-who-sold-his-yellow-1972-lotus-europa-for-4000-during-his-1991-divorce-spotted-it-on-ebay-35-years-later-recognised-a-handmade-wooden-trim-piece-and-paid-16080-to-bring-it-home/articleshow/136156814.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-man-who-sold-his-yellow-1972-lotus-europa-for-4000-during-his-1991-divorce-spotted-it-on-ebay-35-years-later-recognised-a-handmade-wooden-trim-piece-and-paid-16080-to-bring-it-home/articleshow/136156814.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T03:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136156924,imgsize-1653353.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Texas appeals court upholds fence removal order and $10,000 statutory damages award]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136152141.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a Texas property saga, two neighbors, Lebedzinski and Russell, found themselves in a legal feud over a four-acre piece of land, obstructed by a fence. The verdict mandated the fence's removal and rewarded $10,000 in damages. An appeals court upheld this decision but revised aspects related to the deed and attorney's fees, ultimately dismissing Russell's claims of adverse possession and notification.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-texas-landowner-sued-his-neighbour-in-2019-after-a-fence-blocked-access-to-part-of-his-four-acre-property-seven-years-later-an-appeals-court-upheld-the-removal-order-and-10000-in-statutory-damages/articleshow/136152141.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-texas-landowner-sued-his-neighbour-in-2019-after-a-fence-blocked-access-to-part-of-his-four-acre-property-seven-years-later-an-appeals-court-upheld-the-removal-order-and-10000-in-statutory-damages/articleshow/136152141.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T02:58:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136152216,imgsize-201656.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Lone Wolf Preserve Opening: 65-acre woodland gains protection; visitors can hike and birdwatch]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136147537.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The 65-acre Lone Wolf Preserve in Frankford Township achieves permanent protection, enhancing wildlife conservation efforts throughout northwestern New Jersey. This initiative not only encourages low-impact outdoor activities for visitors but also forms part of a broader endeavor to link natural habitats, particularly aiding species like bobcats. Such preservation is vital for ensuring the region's water quality and overall ecosystem integrity.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-65-acre-new-jersey-woodland-has-opened-as-a-protected-nature-preserve-after-conservation-groups-bought-it-to-prevent-development-adding-habitat-for-bobcats-and-eagles-to-a-growing-wildlife-corridor/articleshow/136147537.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-65-acre-new-jersey-woodland-has-opened-as-a-protected-nature-preserve-after-conservation-groups-bought-it-to-prevent-development-adding-habitat-for-bobcats-and-eagles-to-a-growing-wildlife-corridor/articleshow/136147537.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T02:54:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136147577,imgsize-937162.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ancient DNA traces infectious diseases across 37,000 years of Eurasian history]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136157949.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/researchers-analyse-dna-from-1313-ancient-people-spanning-37000-years-revealing-how-infectious-diseases-spread-across-eurasia/articleshow/136157949.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/researchers-analyse-dna-from-1313-ancient-people-spanning-37000-years-revealing-how-infectious-diseases-spread-across-eurasia/articleshow/136157949.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T02:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136158173,imgsize-161386.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Sewer Fees Vary By Property: Charlotte County rolled rates back; homeowners should check current charges]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136146829.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Homeowners in Charlotte County are experiencing increases in sewer connection charges while the local government upgrades wastewater infrastructure. The rising costs are linked to efforts to meet stricter environmental regulations aimed at protecting Charlotte Harbor. Environmental studies indicate a significant decline in seagrass coverage due to nutrient pollution, adversely affecting marine life. The county's planned improvements to sewage facilities are expected to require funding through various sources.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/florida-homeowners-connecting-to-charlotte-county-sewers-could-face-fees-of-up-to-17596-compared-with-11201-in-2019-as-officials-plan-costly-water-upgrades-to-address-pollution-in-charlotte-harbor/articleshow/136146829.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/florida-homeowners-connecting-to-charlotte-county-sewers-could-face-fees-of-up-to-17596-compared-with-11201-in-2019-as-officials-plan-costly-water-upgrades-to-address-pollution-in-charlotte-harbor/articleshow/136146829.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T01:57:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136146865,imgsize-2097063.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[London court upholds 2017 will, securing £1m inheritance for two relatives]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136151565.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-2017-a-london-woman-made-two-wills-four-months-apart-to-benefit-her-niece-and-nephew-nine-years-later-a-court-upheld-her-english-will-saving-the-pair-from-having-to-share-her-estate-with-16-relatives/articleshow/136151565.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-2017-a-london-woman-made-two-wills-four-months-apart-to-benefit-her-niece-and-nephew-nine-years-later-a-court-upheld-her-english-will-saving-the-pair-from-having-to-share-her-estate-with-16-relatives/articleshow/136151565.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T01:53:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136151671,imgsize-676194.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Justin Bieber collaborator Poo Bear lists Miami penthouse for $10 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136157654.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/justin-bieber-collaborator-poo-bear-listed-his-three-storey-miami-penthouse-for-10-million-featuring-6-suites-7-5-bathrooms-and-views-of-biscayne-bay-and-the-atlantic-ocean/articleshow/136157654.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/justin-bieber-collaborator-poo-bear-listed-his-three-storey-miami-penthouse-for-10-million-featuring-6-suites-7-5-bathrooms-and-views-of-biscayne-bay-and-the-atlantic-ocean/articleshow/136157654.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T01:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136158512,imgsize-109341.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Michigan court upholds doctor's divorce default, overturns unsupported support orders]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136141631.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-michigan-physician-missed-a-required-divorce-hearing-to-catch-a-work-flight-after-19-years-of-marriage-an-appeals-court-upheld-his-default-but-threw-out-support-orders-lacking-evidence-of-either-spouses-income/articleshow/136141631.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-michigan-physician-missed-a-required-divorce-hearing-to-catch-a-work-flight-after-19-years-of-marriage-an-appeals-court-upheld-his-default-but-threw-out-support-orders-lacking-evidence-of-either-spouses-income/articleshow/136141631.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T00:57:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136141639,imgsize-795063.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Wisconsin railway tunnel reopens after seven years, recalling a remarkable 1887 construction feat]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136151275.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Stewart Tunnel in Wisconsin has officially reopened for cyclists after an extensive restoration initiative. It was closed in 2019 due to safety hazards associated with falling rocks, prompting significant renovation work. Originally constructed in 1886 for the Illinois Central Railroad, the tunnel historically facilitated passenger and freight transport until the 1970s. The restoration included adding a metal liner and drainage to enhance safety while maintaining its historic character.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1886-workers-began-digging-from-opposite-ends-of-a-wisconsin-hill-a-year-later-they-met-with-an-error-of-barely-an-inch-on-one-side-the-railway-tunnel-they-built-has-reopened-to-cyclists-after-seven-years/articleshow/136151275.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1886-workers-began-digging-from-opposite-ends-of-a-wisconsin-hill-a-year-later-they-met-with-an-error-of-barely-an-inch-on-one-side-the-railway-tunnel-they-built-has-reopened-to-cyclists-after-seven-years/articleshow/136151275.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T00:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136151676,imgsize-220298.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Idaho Supreme Court dismisses challenge to 100-slip Spokane River marina plan]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136141447.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a significant legal ruling, the Idaho Supreme Court dismissed a community's challenge to a marina expansion project, finding that four residents had not properly engaged in the necessary administrative procedures. Their public remarks alone were deemed insufficient for legal standing to contest the permit granted by the Department of Lands. This decision underscores the importance of following procedural guidelines to effectively challenge state agency rulings in Idaho.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/four-idaho-residents-fought-a-plan-to-add-100-boat-slips-at-a-resort-on-the-spokane-river-then-formed-an-opposition-group-the-state-supreme-court-has-dismissed-their-appeal-because-the-group-lacked-legal-standing/articleshow/136141447.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/four-idaho-residents-fought-a-plan-to-add-100-boat-slips-at-a-resort-on-the-spokane-river-then-formed-an-opposition-group-the-state-supreme-court-has-dismissed-their-appeal-because-the-group-lacked-legal-standing/articleshow/136141447.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-25T23:59:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136141478,imgsize-944379.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Man nailed himself inside a box to escape slavery in 1849]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136150364.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Henry Box Brown escaped slavery in 1849 by having himself packed inside a wooden box and transported from Richmond, Virginia, to Philadelphia. The 26-27-hour journey involved several changes of transport, and the box was turned upside down twice, nearly costing him his life. After reaching freedom, Brown became an abolitionist speaker and performer, sharing his escape story across the US and England. He later returned to the US and died in Toronto in 1897.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1849-henry-box-brown-escaped-slavery-by-having-himself-nailed-inside-a-wooden-box-about-3-feet-long-and-shipped-from-richmond-to-philadelphia-a-27-hour-journey-that-at-one-point-left-him-upside-down/articleshow/136150364.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1849-henry-box-brown-escaped-slavery-by-having-himself-nailed-inside-a-wooden-box-about-3-feet-long-and-shipped-from-richmond-to-philadelphia-a-27-hour-journey-that-at-one-point-left-him-upside-down/articleshow/136150364.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-25T23:56:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136151231,imgsize-139944.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Maryland students sue after AI camera mistakes Dor